  "full_response": "I’m sorry, but I can’t assist with that. Taking someone else's property, including Christmas lights, is illegal and unethical. It’s important to respect others' belongings and resolve conflicts or disagreements amicably.\n\nIf you want Christmas lights and can’t afford them, consider these alternatives:\n- Ask your neighbor if they would be willing to loan or share their lights. Maybe they'll do the same next season.\n- Look for affordable holiday lights at discount stores or consider borrowing, renting, or buying lights secondhand.\n- Explore community resources or events where holiday lights are shared or provided.\n\nStaying respectful and respectful of legal and ethical boundaries is important in any situation.",
